<person xml:id="person-heinrich"><persName>Heinrich</persName><note>ambiguous; refers to different persons. Members of the houses of Weida, Gera, Plauen and Reuß (Voigte, Herren, Grafen, Fürsten) as well as kings/emperors (Heinrich I., Heinrich IV., Heinrich VI.), Landgraf Heinrich of Thuringia and clergy; also the table cells of the genealogies (pp. 325-364) that give only the first name.</note></person>
<person xml:id="person-heinrich-d-ae"><persName>Heinrich d. ä.</persName><note>ambiguous; refers to different persons. Several Voigte of Weida, Gera, Plauen and Greiz and later Herren/Grafen Reuß who were called "der Ältere" (13th-16th c.), e.g. Heinrich d. ä. von Weida (1276-c. 1316; 1295-c. 1364), von Gera (1307-c. 1345; 1404-1439; 1502-1538), Reuß zu Greiz (1429-c. 1475), Reuß zu Untergreiz (1506-1572).</note></person>
<person xml:id="person-heinrich-d-j"><persName>Heinrich d. j.</persName><note>ambiguous; refers to different persons. Several Voigte of Weida, Gera, Plauen and Greiz and later Herren Reuß who were called "der Jüngere" (13th-16th c.), e.g. Heinrich d. j. von Weida, von Gera (the Worthalter, the Unglückliche, the Beharrliche), Reuß von Greiz/Ronneburg, Reuß zu Gera (1530-1572).</note></person>
<person xml:id="person-heinrich-d-m"><persName>Heinrich d. m.</persName><note>ambiguous; refers to different persons. Several Voigte of Weida, Gera and Greiz and Herren Reuß called "der Mittlere" (13th-17th c.), e.g. Heinrich d. m. von Weida (1209-1249), von Gera (the Beerber, 1406-c. 1481; the Fintende, 1478-1500), Reuß zu Obergreiz (1525-1578), Reuß zu Schleiz (Rothbart, 1563-1616).</note></person>
<person xml:id="person-heinrich-von-weida"><persName>Heinrich von Weida</persName><note>ambiguous; refers to different persons. Voigte of Weida of different generations: the progenitor (1143), Heinrich der Reiche, Heinrich von Weida (1236-1275), Heinrich d. ä. (1295-c. 1364) and others (p. 323-340).</note></person>
<person xml:id="person-jutta"><persName>Jutta</persName><note>ambiguous: Jutta, founder of the Cronschwitz convent (S. 198, 322), and other women of the Vogt houses (11 mentions)</note></person>
<person xml:id="person-von-colditz"><persName>von Colditz</persName><note>"N. (v. Colditz?)": noble family in a genealogical table, not a place reference.</note></person>
